edgeos-vxlan (0.3.0~rc4+edgeos3.0.1.e50) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release candidate 4: hardware-qualification corrective pass. No new
    feature scope.
  * Reject a ruleset chain that lost its configured rules: every configured
    rule number must be present in the effective chain (vendor <chain>-<n>
    comment format), in addition to the non-empty and terminal
    default-action checks. An unreadable rule list is a configuration-API
    failure, not an empty ruleset. This closes the gap where an EdgeOS 3.0.1
    scripted-session firewall apply could silently reduce a ruleset to its
    default action and still pass verification.
  * Document the hardware-proven EdgeOS 3.0.1 scripted-commit limitation and
    the support boundary (interactive firewall changes; scripted VXLAN
    configuration only against existing, correctly materialized rulesets).
  * Regression: 64 helper + 121 firewall + 93 template + 70 mock = 348
    off-device checks.

 -- Vadim Petrov <vadim@vadimpetrov.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000

edgeos-vxlan (0.3.0~rc3+edgeos3.0.1.e50) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release candidate 3: the RC2 maintainer review's remaining findings.
    No new feature scope.
  * Quiesce a change set that needs more than one sequential vendor
    dispatch operation; keep a single replacement or insertion
    nondisruptive. An operational interface no longer carries an
    intermediate dispatch combination.
  * Install EXIT traps in the helper and reconciler while a firewall
    mutation is in flight. A configuration-API diagnostic after the
    mutation restores the pre-change dispatch and administrative state;
    a recreation runs the normal rollback; if the firewall cannot be
    restored, the interface is left down.
  * Base the capture-failure gate on the previous (effective)
    configuration as well as the candidate. A candidate that removes the
    final attachment no longer makes an enforced interface look
    intentionally unfiltered; an unreadable previous state is
    fail-closed.
  * Verify the terminal rule against the vendor fw.cpp default-action
    format: unconditional vendor comment, accept/drop/reject mapped to
    RETURN/DROP/REJECT, and (for desired state) agreement with the
    configured default-action. Rollback checks shape/verdict consistency
    only. The vendor-owned policy trust boundary is documented.
  * Hardware runbook: account for all runtime-only state (policy
    routing/table, delegated-prefix loopback address, interface-specific
    sysctls), separate native-only structural, router-originated,
    isolated dataplane and external probe evidence, and replace invalid
    multi-chain iptables -S invocations.
  * Add the bounded first-hardware-session sequence
    (docs/v0.3.0-first-hardware-session.md and
    scripts/first-hardware-session.sh): inventory, backup, staging,
    installation and isolated vxlan903 testing only.
  * Regression: 64 helper + 116 firewall + 93 template + 70 mock = 343
    off-device checks. Network-namespace integration 26/26; emulated
    EdgeOS 3.0.1 configuration engine add/replace/remove commits passed
    (evidence in docs/v0.3.0-rc3-evidence.md).

 -- Vadim Petrov <vadim@vadimpetrov.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0000

edgeos-vxlan (0.3.0~rc2+edgeos3.0.1.e50) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release candidate 2: targeted correctness and security review fixes on
    top of RC1. No new feature scope.
  * Fail closed when the live firewall dispatch is ambiguous or unreadable,
    but only when the interface is configured with an attachment; an
    intentionally unfiltered interface is left unchanged.
  * Treat configuration-API diagnostics as fatal instead of reading them as
    "node absent", so a broken read can no longer remove a dispatch or bring a
    disabled interface up.
  * Treat an unreadable administrative state as "may be up" and attempt a
    verified down; never claim a down that was not confirmed.
  * Quiesce the interface across a dispatch removal (the only transition that
    reduces enforcement) and reactivate it only after the previous policy is
    restored and verified. A single replacement/insertion is one atomic
    vendor iptables operation (established by instrumenting the installed
    ubnt-fw binary).
  * Verify hook reachability from INPUT/FORWARD and a terminal default action
    in the target chain, in addition to the exact dispatch.
  * Recover from a failed netdevice deletion after firewall mutation by
    restoring the pre-commit firewall state and administrative state.
  * Hardware runbook rewritten by blast radius; the vxlan41913 migration is a
    quiesced, fail-closed handover (IPv4 in+local and IPv6 in+local); global
    interventions are restricted to a disposable router.
  * Regression: 64 helper + 87 firewall + 90 template + 58 mock = 299
    off-device checks.

 -- Vadim Petrov <vadim@vadimpetrov.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0000

edgeos-vxlan (0.3.0~rc1+edgeos3.0.1.e50) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release candidate 1 for 0.3.0: native firewall integration for routed
    VXLAN interfaces.
  * Add the interfaces vxlan firewall in/out/local subtrees for both IPv4
    (name) and IPv6 (ipv6-name), using the stock ubnt-fw engine and the
    Vyatta interface hook chains.
  * Apply the complete desired attachment set from the VXLAN reconciler
    before any interface mutation, so a failure can be rolled back against
    the pre-change live firewall state.
  * Fail closed: verify that every configured attachment is effective before
    an interface is brought up; take an interface down if a newly requested
    attachment cannot be established; leave it down if the previous firewall
    state cannot be restored during rollback.
  * Remove interface dispatches only after the netdevice has been deleted,
    so a failed deletion cannot expose an operational unfiltered interface.
  * Reject firewall attachments on VXLAN bridge ports: a port attachment does
    not enforce L2-forwarded bridge traffic.  This prevents a misleading
    configuration without enabling global bridge netfilter.
  * Validate ruleset references, address family, interface direction, ruleset
    name syntax and bridge membership at commit time.
  * Extend the package removal guard to refuse removal while live VXLAN
    interfaces exist, in addition to the saved-configuration guard.
  * No kernel module change; the existing vxlan.ko, udp_tunnel.ko and
    CVE-2022-50405 backport are unchanged.
  * Documentation adds the native firewall syntax, underlay/overlay security
    boundaries, routed/bridged semantics, troubleshooting, a generic IPv6
    tunnelbroker example and a hardware acceptance procedure.

 -- Vadim Petrov <vadim@vadimpetrov.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

edgeos-vxlan (0.2.2+edgeos3.0.1.e50) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.2.2: IPv6 VXLAN underlay support on the supported platform.
  * Accept an IPv4 or IPv6 local-ip/remote-ip pair with the same family, and
    reject malformed, prefix-carrying, mixed-family and unusable endpoints
    before anything is changed.
  * Read the tunnel identity from the kernel's local6/remote6 JSON fields so
    IPv6 tunnels reconcile correctly, and compare endpoints canonically so
    equivalent re-spellings stay idempotent.
  * Family-aware default MTU: 1450 over an IPv4 underlay and 1430 over an
    IPv6 underlay; an explicit mtu is always honoured and must be at least 68
    (the kernel's VXLAN minimum) or it is rejected at commit time.
  * Fail closed when the live state cannot be captured completely, and
    restore the captured interface state — including bridge membership, path
    cost and port priority — when a recreation fails.
  * Guard every leaf handler with an identity check.
  * Hardware-validated on the supported platform: native configuration,
    dual-stack dataplane over an IPv6 underlay, recreation, bridging,
    rollback, and save/reboot restoration. See the release notes.
  * The kernel module payloads (vxlan.ko, udp_tunnel.ko), their hashes and
    the CVE-2022-50405 backport are unchanged.

 -- Vadim Petrov <vadim@vadimpetrov.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:40:38 +0000

edgeos-vxlan (0.2.2~rc2+edgeos3.0.1.e50) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release candidate 2 for 0.2.2.
  * Require at least 68 for the VXLAN MTU — the kernel's own minimum for a
    VXLAN device. A value the kernel refuses is now rejected during
    configuration validation instead of after the commit has been applied,
    where the failed commit could leave the active configuration describing an
    interface the kernel never configured.
  * Nothing else changes: the reconciler, the template priorities, the kernel
    modules and the packaging metadata are all untouched.

